  "name": "Boi-bumbá de Parintins (Amazonas toada de boi)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Amazonian ox-drama festival of Parintins, Amazonas, held each June in the Bumbódromo as a contest between the boi Garantido (red) and the boi Caprichoso (blue), grown from a local folguedo into a large staged spectacle with an annual album industry. Its song form, the toada de boi, is sung by a lead singer (levantador de toadas) over a massed percussion section of drums, snares and rattles, called the batucada for Garantido and the marujada for Caprichoso, with keyboards and bass added in recording; a source-unspecified shaker card stands in for the rattles.",
  "recipe": "classic modern boi-bumbá de parintins, groove Percussion, Brazilian branch. single lead single track no stacking. surdo, snare drum, shaker source electronic keyboard unspecified, electric bass. live tracking. tube condenser, 500-series boutique pre, brick-wall limiter, dynamic EQ. 24-bit digital plate reverb digital delay pitch shifter.",
